class StairOutlineNotWritable(APIModel):
    """Not writable: a boundary or a walking line of a stair, as GetDetailsOfElements reads it (leftBoundary, rightBoundary, walkingLine, customWalkingLine, centerWalkingLine). Archicad lays them out itself from the baseline and the flight width, and the API keeps none given: ACAPI_Element_Change refuses a stair memo that holds them (APIERR_GENERAL, also when it is unchanged) or ignores them, ACAPI_Element_ChangeExt does not take stairs (APIERR_BADID), and ACAPI_Element_Create lays them out again, whatever the memo holds (checked on Archicad 29). The walking line stays in the middle of the flight: Archicad 29 keeps walkingLinePosition Center and walkingLineOffset half the flight width whatever is written. An item that gives one is refused with an error, before anything is changed. Change the baseline instead (CreateStairs, RecreateStairs), or flightWidth (ModifyStairs), which moves the boundaries and keeps the walking line in the middle."""
    model_config = ConfigDict(extra="allow")


